From c8c3438d5807f5da6fdf18486cceb54b1d12a92e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Lin <benjamin-jw.lin@mediatek.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Jan 2026 10:53:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: hostapd: unify vendor commands for different chip
 generation

This commit squashes following commits for conciseness.

mtk: hostapd: prevent casting bss->ctx to hostapd_data in nl80211

Since the bss->ctx might be the type of struct hostapd_data or struct
wpa_supplicant, casting the bss->ctx to struct hostapd_data leads to
crash if bss->ctx is actually the type of wpa_supplciant.

For example, wpa_s fails mesh interface setup and crashes due to the
casting.

To prevent casting bss->ctx to hostapd_data, this commit does the
following changes.

For the following driver operations, the "radio_idx" is changed to a
function parameter and passed by the caller:
- configure_edcca_enable
- configure_edcca_threshold
- get_edcca
- csi_set
- csi_dump
- dfs_tx_mode

For the following driver operations, all necessary data are grouped in a
struct named "struct wpa_driver_mu_params"
- mu_ctrl
- mu_dump

Signed-off-by: Michael-CY Lee <michael-cy.lee@mediatek.com>

mtk: hostapd: refactor muru_manual_config to unify connac2 and connac3

Refactor muru_manual_config structure names to unify connac2 and connac3.

Signed-off-by: Howard Hsu <howard-yh.hsu@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Benjamin Lin <benjamin-jw.lin@mediatek.com>

mtk: hostapd: Update MAC address handling in vendor policies

Signed-off-by: Peter Chiu <chui-hao.chiu@mediatek.com>

mtk: hostapd: unify vendor command for different chip generation

This patch is part of a series to unify vendor commands across chip
generations.

Integrate Wi-Fi 6 vendor commands with Wi-Fi 7/8 and use
VENDOR_SUBCMD_ABI_CONNAC2 to split for some old Wi-Fi 6 paths.

Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
